WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.672
Anika: Requests are draining without new buildup. Support can report order processing recovered.

2
00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:14.112
Hannah: Include which functions remain restricted now. Reports are still unavailable to users.

3
00:00:14.112 --> 00:00:20.833
Raj: Connection checkout time stays near baseline. The cleanup canary passed cancellation checks.

4
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:27.841
Priya: Okay, no full repair claim, right? The temporary workaround still includes limits.

5
00:00:27.841 --> 00:00:34.897
Lukas: Yes. Expand the fix in batches. Observe each batch before relaxing limits.

6
00:00:34.897 --> 00:00:40.873
Anika: What's the ETA for report recovery? Maybe tomorrow after the query review.

7
00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:48.313
Hannah: Call that an estimate, not commitment. Include the escalation path for regressions.

8
00:00:48.313 --> 00:00:54.818
Priya: So, circle back in thirty minutes. Earlier if waiting requests start rising.

9
00:00:54.818 --> 00:01:01.658
Lukas: I'll watch accepted throughput during expansion. Low errors with fewer orders isn't recovery.

10
00:01:01.658 --> 00:01:08.210
Raj: Agreed, throughput matches the expected demand. I'll attach that evidence to support.

